  "lyrics": [
    {
      "tag": "VERSE 1",
      "lines": [
        "Five-fifteen and the sky's the colour of a bruise on a peach,",
        "I-10 humming like a hymn nobody bothered to teach,",
        "Mama had the radio on the gospel station low,",
        "I had the window cracked to hear the trains on Navigation go.",
        "Warehouse wall on Harrisburg, somebody painted STILL HERE,",
        "same two words in the same spot for the last eleven years,",
        "I clock in with a thermos and a head full of lines,",
        "foreman think I'm counting pallets, I'm just counting the rhymes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "HOOK",
      "lines": [
        "Concrete choir, singing on the feeder road,",
        "every horn a harmony, every siren holding notes,",
        "nobody asked us but we sing it anyway,",
        "concrete choir, holding the city up all day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "VERSE 2",
      "lines": [
        "Dispatch in my ear, said swing it by the port,",
        "forty minutes out to Baytown if the traffic keeps it short,",
        "I know every pothole on the loop like I know my brother's laugh,",
        "know the truck on Wayside sells out of barbacoa by half past.",
        "Uncle used to say a city's just a choir with no conductor,",
        "everybody's got a part and everybody's out of tune together,",
        "so I sing mine low, keep it in the cab, keep it on the clock,",
        "and when the shift ends, shit, I'm still humming in the parking lot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "HOOK",
      "lines": [
        "Concrete choir, singing on the feeder road,",
        "every horn a harmony, every siren holding notes,",
        "nobody asked us but we sing it anyway,",
        "concrete choir, holding the city up all day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "BRIDGE, SPOKEN",
      "lines": [
        "Everybody out here is singing something.",
        "You just got to roll the window down."
      ]
    },
    {
